course: dictionary
lesson: 4042
title: One word, two meanings: gem
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. Gem has two main meanings. The first is a real stone: a beautiful, valuable stone, such as a diamond, ruby or emerald, cut and polished to make jewellery sparkle.
explain: The second meaning is about a person or thing that is especially good or special. «You're a gem» is a kind way to say thank you. If someone says it after you help them, they mean you are a special person.
explain: Gem also appears in phrases like «a hidden gem», which means a great place that few people know about. To check the meaning, ask yourself: is this about rocks and treasure, or about someone being kind? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it makes sense.
fact: A gem is a beautiful, valuable stone, such as a diamond, ruby or emerald.
fact: Most gems are minerals that grew as crystals deep in the Earth.
fact: Gems are cut and polished so that they sparkle.
fact: «You're a gem» means you are a kind or special person.
fact: «A hidden gem» means a great place that few people know about.
exercise: «Most gems are minerals that grew as crystals deep in the Earth.» Which meaning of gem is used here? | A kind thank you | A great place few people know | A loud noise in the mountains | *A beautiful, valuable stone
exercise: Ms Lee says, «Sam, you're a gem for helping me carry the bags!» What does gem mean? | A cold, hard rock | *A kind and special person | A cloth bag for shopping | A shiny stone for a ring
exercise: «Never buy gems, coins or loot boxes in a game without a parent's permission; small purchases add up fast.» Why should you ask a parent first? | Games are always free | *Small purchases can add up to a lot of real money | Gems make the game run slower | Parents enjoy buying games
test: «We found a hidden gem: a tiny cafe by the river that almost nobody knew.» What does hidden gem mean here? | *A great place few people know about | A cave full of stones | A secret box of coins | A broken old boat
test: «In-app money is real money: gems, coins and skins are paid for from a real bank account.» What does this tell you about gems in games? | They make your character invisible | They are given away free at school | *They are paid for with real money | They can only be found in rocks
exam: «A girl downloaded a cheat for an online game from a site that promised free gems; it put a virus on the family computer.» What lesson does this story teach? | Cheats always make games better | Viruses are a kind of gem | *A free offer can be a trap | Computers need gems to work
